B.VT=new A.dc(0,18,"In early 19th-century Edinburgh, medical research was at the cutting edge of science.")
B.VQ=new A.dc(18,38,"Lecturers needed human cadavers for dissection, creating an immense, lucrative demand for bodies.")
B.VU=new A.dc(38,64,"Resurrection Men crept into churchyards at night to dig up newly buried corpses and sell them.")
B.VH=new A.dc(64,96,'Families invented "mortsafes": massive iron cages locked over graves to protect their deceased loved ones.')
B.VF=new A.dc(96,130,"After six to eight weeks of decomposition, the cage was removed and rented to another family.")
B.VV=new A.dc(130,180,"These iron cages before you are authentic survivals of Edinburgh's grave-robbing panic!")
B.IP=s([B.VT,B.VQ,B.VU,B.VH,B.VF,B.VV],t.hB)
B.VD=new A.kq("stop-a","Stop A","The Mortsafes","Head to the Mortsafes","Use the map below to find your way to Stop A. Look for the iron cages near the south side of the Kirk.","You should see these iron cages in front of you. Press play to hear the story behind them.","assets/audio/mortsafes.mp3","assets/images/screen-stop-a_photo.jpg",null,B.ju,1,'In early 19th-century Edinburgh, medical teaching and anatomical research were at the cutting edge of science. But medical lecturers needed human cadavers for dissection, creating an immense, lucrative demand.\n\nEnter the "Resurrection Men" \u2014 grave robbers who would creep into churchyards in the dead of night to dig up newly buried bodies and sell them to anatomy professors.\n\nTo protect their deceased loved ones, Edinburgh families invented "mortsafes": massive iron cages or heavy stone vaults placed over fresh graves. These remained locked over the coffin for six to eight weeks until the body had decomposed enough to be useless for medical dissection, after which the cage would be removed and rented to another family.\n\nThese iron cages you see before you are authentic survivals of Edinburgh\'s grave-robbing panic!',B.IP)
